# SDK (`sdk/`)

- Never break user applications if backend is misconfigured, unavailable, or slow.
- Keep hot path async/non-blocking and dependency-light; preserve bounded queue/drop behavior.
- Preserve silent-failure defaults (except explicit debug modes) and scrub sensitive data before send.
- Keep public API stable and typed; align names and behavior with `DEVELOPMENT.md`.
- Framework adapters live as `lumonox.<framework>.middleware` (FastAPI and Django; FastAPI ships in the default install, Django behind the `[django]` extra) and reuse the framework-agnostic `lumonox.core.*` send path — never fork the dispatcher / scrubbing / event-shape / config-builder logic per adapter. See `sdk/docs/adapters.md` for the adapter contract.
- Run deterministic targeted SDK tests under `sdk/tests/` for touched behavior.

## Rule self-review

When this rule materially guided the task, follow **Rules self-review** in `lumonox-execution.mdc` and apply it to this file.
